 #:seon.task{:name "alias-and-require-as-retarget-silently"
  :kind :function
  :intent "In SCI, (require '[clojure.set :as x]) after x -> clojure.string returns nil and retargets the alias; so does (alias 'x 'clojure.walk) (sci-alias is a bare assoc-in, namespaces.cljc:478-486). Clojure refuses a different target (Namespace.java:257-258, \"Alias x already exists in namespace .., aliasing ..\"). The silent retarget makes stored definitions position-dependent and is the source of the digest refusals in the alias design probes. Correct: alias and require :as with a different target refuse as Clojure does, ns-unalias! being the guarded path (SCI runs ns-unalias itself); a refer replacement stays legal (a warning in Clojure). Related issue docs/seon/issues/reload-refuses-an-alias-retargeted-by-the-new-source.md. Proof: evaluating (alias 'x 'clojure.set) after x -> clojure.string answers a refusal error and leaves the alias unchanged."
  :must-read #{my.program/ns-unalias!}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/s5-admission/alias-design.md" "docs/seon/issues/reload-refuses-an-alias-retargeted-by-the-new-source.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "merge-tools-throw-instead-of-returning"
             :kind :function
             :intent "propose-merge! and prepare-merge! are returning tools but throw: propose-merge! on a branch whose contract names an agent-registered schema throws :malli.core/invalid-schema out of `seon.test/run` (seon.test/check-fails-on-agent-registered-schemas), and prepare-merge! of a test-only new namespace throws entity-id/missing. Done when each returns its error map naming the failing proof or row, regressions through MCP SCI."
             :must-read #{my.program/propose-merge! my.program/prepare-merge!}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/specs/merge.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "root-cannot-diff-a-proposal"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`my.program/diff` compares only my own branch with my cluster head; root reviewing a proposal has no entrance to diff the proposal's branch against the head it would merge onto. The dogfood needed JVM mode, seon.operator.runtime/running-instances for the store, and `seon.cluster.source/compare-branch` (174 ms). Done when (`my.program/diff` {`:seon.task/merge` m}) answers the merge diff value (docs/seon/specs/merge.md §2) from root's context."
             :must-read #{my.program/diff seon.cluster.source/compare-branch}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/specs/merge.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "accept-cannot-retire-a-hosted-proposers-branch"
             :kind :function
             :intent "accept-merge!'s detached retire of the proposing branch fails while the proposer's hosted agent holds a connection ('branch :agent-099e88cb509c still has a connection in this process'), recorded as an open fault produced by `my.program/accept-merge!` (2026-10-08); the branch stays in the roster. Done when accepting a hosted agent's proposal releases its acquisition and retires its branch, regression through MCP SCI."
             :must-read #{my.program/accept-merge! my.agent/retire-branch!}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/specs/merge.md"}}
