             :intent "(`my.program/ns-unmap!` 'seon.help-test 'help-teaches-how-a-deftest-names-its-task), the two-argument call of `clojure.core/ns-unmap`, answered \"refused argument 0 `context`: expected :my.program/context (a map), got a symbol seon.help-test\" with the world's whole context schema as its problem (fanout-3 run, default 324461975, 2026-10-09); the call that works takes one qualified symbol. Done when a two-symbol call either unmaps that namespace's name as Clojure does or is refused as an arity error naming the one-symbol form."
