             :kind :function
             :intent "Agent fan4-empty (fanout-4, default 97f2b2ac3, 2026-10-09) added the alias string for clojure.string in seon.error at its REPL; the alias joined the stored seon.error namespace row (its definition digest changed), and (`clojure.core/ns-unalias` 'seon.error 'string) left the row unchanged, so `my.program/diff` kept listing the namespace as changed and `my.program/write-branch!` refused the file. Done when an alias removed with ns-unalias leaves the namespace row as it was, or the diff names the alias as the change and offers the form that removes it."
